From a9d56a4fbe344c8319d4908525579b4e6207043a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 00:53:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Lower population threshold: compare against whoever has
 checked in so far

Instead of gating the z-score level behind a fixed 'wait for 30 people'
rule, it now always compares against the current pool (minimum 2, needed
for a non-trivial standard deviation) and shows the headcount ('berdasarkan
N peserta' on the dashboard, 'dibanding N peserta lain' on the participant
result) so viewers can judge reliability themselves as the sample grows,
rather than seeing nothing until an arbitrary threshold is hit.
---
